% Generated by scripts/generate_yytree_help.R; edit that source instead.
\name{yytree}
\alias{yytree}
\title{
Create a tree plot specification
}
\description{
Create a plot specification from one tree without starting Java or opening a window.
}
\usage{
yytree(tree, width = 1000, height = 800, blank_top = 20, blank_left = 40,
    blank_bottom = 80, blank_right = 40)
}
\arguments{
\item{tree}{Required. One \code{hclust} or \code{ape::phylo} object, one Newick string, or one Newick file path. A character value naming an existing file is read as UTF-8; otherwise it is parsed as Newick. Supply exactly one tree.}
\item{width}{One finite positive integer: logical canvas width in pixels. Default 1000.}
\item{height}{One finite positive integer: logical canvas height in pixels. Default 800.}
\item{blank_top}{Finite nonnegative top margin in logical pixels. Default 20.}
\item{blank_left}{Finite nonnegative left margin in logical pixels. Default 40.}
\item{blank_bottom}{Finite nonnegative bottom margin in logical pixels. Default 80.}
\item{blank_right}{Finite nonnegative right margin in logical pixels. Default 40.}
}
\details{
The initial display uses rectangular layout 1 and hides leaf labels. Add \code{leaf_labels()} to show them.

Input leaf order is retained. \code{hclust} branch lengths are parent minus child merge heights; negative or nonfinite lengths are rejected. A \code{phylo} without branch lengths uses length 1 for each edge. Newick labels retain spaces, Unicode and quoted punctuation. Leaf names must be nonempty and unique; an entirely unnamed tree receives numeric names. Trees must be connected with one root and nonnegative finite branch lengths.

Widths, heights and margins describe the logical canvas, not the preview window. Space for labels, tracks and legends is reserved in addition to these margins. If insufficient drawing space remains, printing reports an error; increase the canvas dimensions.

The result is an ordinary serializable R value. Creating or saving it does not require a configured Java runtime.
}
\value{
A \code{yytree} value containing the tree, logical canvas and an initially empty layer list.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{layout}}, \code{\link{leaf_labels}}, \code{\link{+.yytree}}, \code{\link{print.yytree}}, \code{\link{yytree-package}}
}
\examples{
tree <- "((A:1,B:2):1,C:3);"
p <- yytree(tree)
q <- yytree(hclust(dist(USArrests)), width = 1200) + leaf_labels()
stopifnot(inherits(p, "yytree"), length(p$layers) == 0)
# Displaying a plot requires config_yytree(); see ?print.yytree.

}
